><p>Chest CT on admission (A) and follow-up after 2 months (B) reveals markedly improved ground glass opacity and air space consolidation in both lungs.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="aair-2-144-g002"/></fig><fig id="F3" position="float"><label>Fig. 3</label><caption><p>(A) Bronchoalveolar lavage fluid showed more than 25% eosinophils. (Wright stain, &#x000d7;400). (B) Lung biopsy specimen on the third day shows that many inflammatory cells are present in the alveolar spaces and septae, which are admixed with fibrous exudates. The majority of the infiltrated cells are eosinophils (Hematoxylin-eosin stain, &#x000d7;400).</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="aair-2-144-g003"/></fig></floats-group></article>